Runs every platform you have set up, and rebuilds them on change.

By default this is every platform in `app.platforms` that this machine can run: the web app served from `dist/`, and each native app on this machine, in every booted iOS Simulator, and on every attached Android device or emulator. When no simulator or emulator is running, one is started. Native apps swap in each rebuilt guest without being reinstalled.

Usage: leptoskit dev [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --open
          Open the browser after the web server starts

      --port <PORT>
          Serve the web app on a different port than the configuration says

      --platform <PLATFORM>
          Run only this platform; repeat it to run several. Fails when this machine cannot run a platform named here

      --device <DEVICE>
          Run iOS and Android only on this device: a simulator's name or UDID, or an adb serial. Repeat it for several. A named simulator that is shut down boots

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
